    Bug 1953353 - Unify coding patterns in xpcshell tests. r=mkmelin

    Our xpcshell extension tests have evolved and certain patterns have been
    established over time, but not all tests have been updated. Most new
    tests are created by copying an older test, which bleeds old patterns
    into new tests.

    This patch unifies our xpcshell tests:
    * use strict mode
    * use `add_setup()` to define the test environment
    * reduce code in global scope and move it into `add_setup()` (for example calls to `registerCleanupFunction()`)
    * use `var` to declare/import system modules
    * use `const` or `let` for global functions and use the `g` prefix (or all caps)
    * add licence header to all files
    * always use helper functions for basic account operations

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D241152

